WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.120
A surprising Shanks moment in "One Piece Film:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.703
Red" is sure to please fans&nbsp;
of the mega-popular anime.

00:00:06.703 --> 00:00:10.680
“One Piece Film: Red” premiered in&nbsp;
Japanese theaters in August of 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.240
and almost immediately reached some major&nbsp;
milestones at the box office. A little more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.780
than one month after its release,&nbsp;
it earned more than 15 billion yen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.980
placing it among some of the highest-grossing&nbsp;
films in Japanese box office history.

00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:24.929
"Let's do this!"

00:00:25.027 --> 00:00:28.860
While this latest movie is effectively&nbsp;
a non-canonical side story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.820
its value to veteran “One Piece”&nbsp;
fans lies partially in how “Film:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.460
Red” incorporates certain characters for the first&nbsp;
time by including Red-Haired Shanks and his pirate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.740
crew in a non-flashback storyline, alongside&nbsp;
longtime protagonist Luffy and his shipmates.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:49.020
Shanks’ appearance in “Film: Red” is notable in&nbsp;
and of itself, in that Shanks is introduced as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.580
a key character at the series' outset, but has yet&nbsp;
to factor into the story of "One Piece" since then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.380
outside of some peripheral involvement. As it&nbsp;
turns out, "Film: Red" not only includes a rare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.060
Shanks appearance, but demonstrates the power of&nbsp;
his Conqueror's Haki for the first time as well.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.880
Just after the big, climactic battle in "One&nbsp;
Piece Film: Red," some marine admirals attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.440
to approach Uta and possibly apprehend Shanks&nbsp;
as well, whose bounty is one of the highest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.640
of all living pirates. In response, Shanks&nbsp;
unleashes a massive outpouring of energy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.200
that collapses every Navy grunt and even&nbsp;
brings some Vice Admirals to their knees.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.300
While Shanks’ use of his Conqueror’s Haki&nbsp;
doesn’t significantly affect the two Admirals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.860
they decide that a battle against Shanks would&nbsp;
be unwise, given that civilians are present,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.666
and wielding such great power in the midst of&nbsp;
noncombatants may result in unwanted casualties.

00:01:37.035 --> 00:01:40.658
In this scene, Shanks’ Conqueror’s&nbsp;
Haki is effectively a warning shot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.658 --> 00:01:46.020
meaning that the full range of his powers remains&nbsp;
largely unknown. Nevertheless, Shanks’ defense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.340
Uta is the closest look at Shanks’ strength&nbsp;
from throughout all of “One Piece” thus far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.780
be it in anime canon, a non-canonical&nbsp;
side story, or the original manga series.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.640
In the world of “One Piece," Haki is a catch-all&nbsp;
term for a few different kinds of extrasensory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.020
abilities that can only manifest in extreme&nbsp;
conditions. Technically, the Skypiea Arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.240
introduces Haki for the first time as a power&nbsp;
the residents of its Sky Island call Mantra.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:13.020
Then, just before the time skip that&nbsp;
bisects the first and second halves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.700
of "One Piece," retired pirate Rayleigh&nbsp;
instructs Luffy on how to utilize Haki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.020
and his lesson serves as the fans' first proper&nbsp;
introduction to Haki in its various forms.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.900
Rayleigh teaches Luffy about Observation Haki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.500
which allows its user advanced&nbsp;
forms of perception; Armament Haki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.820
which can bolster its user’s attack and&nbsp;
defense; and Conqueror's Haki, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:38.143
effectively an expression of willpower that can&nbsp;
physically overwhelm those of weaker disposition.

00:02:38.143 --> 00:02:42.900
Hypothetically, anybody can learn to wield&nbsp;
Observation and Armament Haki, but Conqueror's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.000
Haki is a rarity, available only to those lucky&nbsp;
enough to win the genetic lottery, so to speak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.040
Luffy and Shanks are both capable of wielding&nbsp;
Conqueror’s Haki, and Shanks even lets out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.440
weak version of his Conqueror's Haki when he meets&nbsp;
with Whitebeard just prior to the Marineford Arc.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.600
It’s only in “Film: Red,” however, that Shanks&nbsp;
lets his Conqueror’s Haki loose, giving viewers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.100
a look at the true extent of his power for the&nbsp;
first time. Tease though it may be, the inclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:13.200
of Shanks’ Conqueror’s Haki in “One Piece Film:&nbsp;
Red” is significant in that it demystifies — even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.940
if just barely — a character shrouded in questions&nbsp;
ever since his introduction at the start of “One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.886
Piece,” and continuing through the nearly 25&nbsp;
years between then and his “Film: Red” debut.

00:03:23.009 --> 00:03:27.300
A Reddit thread from September of 2022,&nbsp;
for example, lists five options in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.840
poll asking users to vote what they&nbsp;
would most like to know about Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.960
each of which is a separate question&nbsp;
raised about his character at some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.070
point in “One Piece.” In the most-upvoted&nbsp;
response in that thread, one user wrote,

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:42.480
“Where is Shanks, who is Shanks, why is&nbsp;
Shanks, when is Shanks, which is Shanks?”

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.120
Meanwhile, the director in charge&nbsp;
of dubbing “One Piece Film:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.420
Red,” Anthony Bowling, highlighted&nbsp;
Shanks’ involvement as one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.480
movie’s highlights in an Anime&nbsp;
News Network interview, saying,

00:03:51.578 --> 00:03:54.964
"Fans are going to love what they&nbsp;
get to see with him and his crew."

00:03:54.964 --> 00:03:59.280
Though Shanks may not be the focus of “Film:&nbsp;
Red,” the fact that he actively engages in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.721
fight alongside Luffy and his friends marks&nbsp;
a “One Piece” first, imbuing the mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.721 --> 00:04:07.801
character with some much-needed context as&nbsp;
“One Piece” inches toward its final stretch.

